    "body": "Hi echasnovski,\n\nthe qfl and loclist `[q` and `[l` bindings do not respect/exactly mirror quickfix/loclist navigation.\n\nthis is because they do not respect (i.e. skip over) the \"valid\" tags quick/loclist entries may have.",
    "closed_at": "2026-11-08T00:46:22Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nWhile this is the first time I encounter the \"invalid\" quickfix entries, the feature parity with `:cnext` / `:lnext` was never the goal of these 'mini.bracketed' targets. So I'd appreciate first opening an issue about this (as described in the 'CONTRIBUTING.md').\r\n\r\nI don't think I immediately agree that \"skipping\" behavior of `:cnext` / `:lnext` is a good thing to follow. I'll take a closer look a bit later.",
            "created_at": "2026-11-07T18:10:57Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2594#issuecomment-6711142964",
